	id: "1F2D08F4FEF1CEDC"
	order_index: 15
	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"The energy system in GregTech is far less simple than that of other tech mods."
				""
				"GregTech's energy unit is EU, which is different from the FE used by other modules."
				""
				"The EU mechanism is not similar to real-world electricity:"
				"Power = voltage x current"
				"Energy = Power x Time"
				"Resistance is modeled as cable loss in GregTech"
				""
				"GregTech is defined as follows:"
				"- EU is the unit of energy."
				"- EU/t is the power."
				"- A (ampere) is the current."
				"- V (volt) is voltage, which is called LV, MV,HVin the game...because these are gameplay-related values ​​(technically:LV= 32V = 32EU/t/A)."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_battery_buffer_4x"
			id: "7F97BED1B9552E5E"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "21A127B9A78F381C"
					item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7B797503EA800D59"
					title: "Basic settings"
					type: "checkmark"
				}
			]
			x: -3.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"In GregTech, electricity is transmitted in \\\"packets\\\". The size of each packet is equivalent to its voltage level."
				""
				"Taking the LV packet as an example, this \\\"packet\\\" will carry 32 EU, multiple blocks are able to generate these EU packets, and the packet will only be generated when the destination can be reached."
				""
				"Every tick (1/20th of a second or 0.05 seconds), the EU \\\"package\\\" attempts to transfer from energy producer to consumer."
				""
				"These \\\"packages\\\" have two parameters: the voltage level (V) determined by the producer rating, and the current (A), which determines how much power can actually be transmitted."
				""
				"Energy is transferred only when the complete \\\"packet\\\" of amps can be received. You may notice that your machines are just below full EU capacity - they will only accept EU if they are missing at least 1A of input voltage."
				""
				"If a machine receives a voltage higher than its voltage rating, it will explode, but any excess current will have no adverse effects because the machine only draws as much as it needs."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Machine explosions would also normally destroy terrain, but that feature is disabled in this pack."
				""
				"In short, energy is transmitted in the form of \\\"packets\\\", which is 32EU for LV, 128EU for MV... and so on. Due to cable loss, the actual energy received by the machine may be lower than the energy sent."
				""
				"Machine energy input is limited by voltage and current, so an MV machine connected to an LV line with an input current of 1A will never accept more than 32EU/t."
				""
				"You can still run an MV machine on the LV line, but only if the recipe power is low enough, or if you have a medium voltage battery in the machine's charging slot, the machine will only accept 1A when idle, so the battery will charge at the maximum rate of 32EU/t."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_transformer_1a"
			id: "0CC922B821305906"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "6AACFA4A99B6EF47"
					item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "34D8E6B118290930"
					title: "energy transfer"
					type: "checkmark"
				}
			]
			x: -1.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Transmitting EU is done via directly connected wires or cables."
				""
				"Wires are a poor choice because they can shock you and have high wire loss, so you need to use insulated cable."
				""
				"Line loss means you have to move your machine closer to your generator, but this only becomes an issue early in the game."
				""
				"GregTech's cable loss means that each cable block's EU packet transmission reduces its stored EU."
				""
				"For example, if the wire loss of a tin cable is 1, for a 4-meter cable connected from a basic internal combustion engine, the voltage at the end is only 28 EU/t, which is less than the 30 EU/t of the average LV machine power. Therefore, a working machine may trip after a few seconds."
				""
				"But there is no need to worry here, if you browse the mission statement, you will find that there is cheap superconducting in the early stage and wireless in the later stage, thus completely avoiding this problem."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:tin_single_cable"
			id: "4A7E19EF14D3C072"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "0742E14D9F82B5DA"
					item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "6C551BD24A83AB3F"
					title: "Cable transmission"
					type: "checkmark"
				}
			]
			x: 1.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"In GregTech, each small generator produces a voltage level of 1A, but here the output current of the small generators is greatly increased."
				""
				"If a machine requires 32EU/t, a 32EU \\\"package\\\" will be sent every tick."
				""
				"A LV battery box with 4 cells can produce 4 amps of LV (128EU/t)."
				""
				"The generic machine is configured to draw 2 amps, other machines have specific amp inputs, which are described in their tooltips."
				""
				"Trying to transport more amps than the limit will burn your cables."
				""
				"Ampere only draws via a cable directly connected to the producer and consumer, and only draws when the consumer is running."
				""
				"This means you can safely reduce the thickness of your cables in some places."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_diode"
			id: "4F7A3702787F86A7"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "12DB6E7A8A385246"
					item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "007D09C6CE7CB00B"
					title: "current"
					type: "checkmark"
				}
			]
			x: 3.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Overclocking is a mechanism that occurs when you try to run a recipe in a machine with a higher power than the recipe itself, the recipe will use more energy, but the recipe time will be reduced based on the level you are overclocking."
				""
				"Some machines have a side menu to set the maximum voltage level it can overclock to, click this to cycle through all available voltages and select a limit."
				""
				"One overclock is allowed for every four times the supplied power above the recipe power. Each overclock means: 2x recipe speed, 4x power consumption, 2x total energy cost, called&blossy overclock &r. Most machines use lossy overclocking."
				""
				"However, ULV formulas (even 2EU/t grinder formulas) will not be overclocked in LV machines, so they will only use LV-level electrical power when reaching MV (grinder formulas generally use 32EU/t only when HV is obtained)."
				""
				"The corresponding concept is&dlossless overclocking &r, 4x recipe speed, 4x power consumption, 1x total energy cost."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:clock"
			id: "5535934109A12B5D"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "31ED6CE96AA0C0E8"
					item: "gtceu:cupronickel_credit"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4DB7B7FC0312D572"
					title: "Overclocking"
					type: "checkmark"
				}
			]
			x: 5.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Of course, voltages can be converted between voltages using a transformer. The transformer can only convert between two adjacent voltage levels, with both boost and buck modes. In boost mode, the voltage and 4x current will be converted to a higher voltage and 1x current, and vice versa in buck mode."
				""
				"There are four types of transformers: ordinary, advanced, high-current and high-energy transformers. The ordinary transformer is 1A<-->4A, the advanced transformer is 2A<-->8A, the high-current transformer is 4A<-->16A, and the high-energy transformer is 16A<-->64A. The red side of the transformer corresponds to low voltage, and the green side corresponds to high voltage."
				""
				"The multi-block machine active transformer unlocked in the LuV stage can support the conversion between any voltage and any current, automatically boost/step down the voltage, and can replace all ordinary transformers in high voltage and high current environments in the middle and later stages."
				""
				"But the real purpose of the active is to bend the laser."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:active_transformer"
			id: "010CF028448C17A9"
			rewards: [
				{
